WEBVTT

00:00:00.480 --> 00:00:04.840
Select an operating-system image that supports the accelerator and the intended framework.

00:00:04.840 --> 00:00:08.210
A provider image with validated drivers and CUDA can shorten setup,

00:00:08.210 --> 00:00:10.450
but its versions still need to match the application.

00:00:10.450 --> 00:00:14.845
Verify the GPU at the operating-system level, then run a small framework operation.

00:00:14.845 --> 00:00:18.290
Detection alone does not prove that model inference or training will use acceleration

00:00:18.290 --> 00:00:18.880
correctly.

00:00:18.880 --> 00:00:21.440
Containers can package the application, libraries,

00:00:21.440 --> 00:00:25.580
and model server into a repeatable unit while relying on a compatible host driver and GPU

00:00:25.580 --> 00:00:26.255
runtime.

00:00:26.255 --> 00:00:29.075
Pin container images to known versions or digests.

00:00:29.075 --> 00:00:31.040
If using Python environments directly,

00:00:31.040 --> 00:00:33.880
isolate dependencies and record exact package versions.

00:00:33.880 --> 00:00:37.830
Notebooks are effective for exploration but should not become undocumented production

00:00:37.830 --> 00:00:38.610
servers.

00:00:38.610 --> 00:00:40.640
Secure SSH before beginning model work.

00:00:40.640 --> 00:00:44.225
Restrict source addresses, use managed or short-lived keys where possible,

00:00:44.225 --> 00:00:46.089
and remove default or stale credentials.

00:00:46.089 --> 00:00:48.900
Bind notebooks and model servers to private interfaces.

00:00:48.900 --> 00:00:52.555
Reach them through an authenticated gateway or secure tunnel rather than opening

00:00:52.555 --> 00:00:54.115
administrative ports broadly.

00:00:54.115 --> 00:00:58.600
Keep API keys and model-repository tokens out of scripts, notebooks, and machine images.

00:00:58.600 --> 00:01:03.270
Begin with a simple manual path: start the instance, verify acceleration, load one model,

00:01:03.270 --> 00:01:05.813
run one representative request, and shut down.

00:01:05.813 --> 00:01:09.160
Record commands, versions, ports, storage mounts, and expected output.

00:01:09.160 --> 00:01:10.320
Once the path is proven,

00:01:10.320 --> 00:01:14.156
automate it with reviewed setup scripts or images and test on a fresh rental.

00:01:14.156 --> 00:01:17.970
Reproducible setup saves billable troubleshooting time and makes an instance replaceable

00:01:17.970 --> 00:01:19.050
instead of precious.
